-of-midterms-report-jd-vance-rnc-iowa-florida-texas-alaska-oklahoma-alabama-ohio-nebraska-ken-paxton-dan-sullivan-pete-ricketts">READ MORE NEWS</a></div></div></div></div></div><button aria-label="expand alert container" class="Alerts_expander__hYQw_"></button><div class="Alerts_controlsWrapper__E2nII"><button class="Alerts_dismiss__oe3zs"><svg class="Alerts_closeIcon__ArjET" height="18px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 17 18" width="17px" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><title>Close</title><g fill="none" fill-rule="evenodd" stroke="none" stroke-width="1"><g fill="#fff" transform="translate(-271.000000, -437.000000)"><g transform="translate(249.000000, 416.000000)"><g transform="translate(21.000000, 21.000000)"><g><rect height="2" id="Rectangle-2-Copy" transform="translate(9.500000, 9.000000) rotate(-45.000000) translate(-9.500000, -9.000000) " width="23" x="-2" y="8"></rect><rect height="2" id="Rectangle-2-Copy-3" transform="translate(9.500000, 9.000000) rotate(45.000000) translate(-9.500000, -9.000000) " width="23" x="-2" y="8"></rect></g></g></g></g></g></svg></button></div></div></div></div><div class="layout_style_pageContents__wCLzZ"><main class="layout_style_mainContent__ZTKzO" id="maincontent" tabindex="-1"><script>(self.__next_s=self.__next_s||[]).push([0,{"children":"(function () {\n    var assignment = {\"name\":\"Taboola Deeper Dive\",\"variant\":\"active\"};\n    var assignments = Array.isArray(window.ldExperiments) ? window.ldExperiments : [];\n    var existingIndex = assignments.findIndex(function (item) {\n        return item.name === assignment.name;\n    });\n    var isNewAssignment = existingIndex === -1\n        || assignments[existingIndex].variant !== assignment.variant;\n\n    if (existingIndex === -1) {\n        assignments.push(assignment);\n    } else {\n        assignments[existingIndex] = assignment;\n    }\n\n    window.ldExperiments = assignments;\n    window.ldExpName = assignment.name;\n    window.ldExpVar = assignment.variant;\n\n    if (isNewAssignment) {\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\n        window.dataLayer.push({\n            event: \"experiment_assignment\",\n            experiment_name: assignment.name,\n            experiment_variant: assignment.variant\n        });\n    }\n}());","id":"deeper-dive-experiment-tracking"}])</script><script>(self.__next_s=self.__next_s||[]).push([0,{"children":"(function () {\n    var assignment = {\"name\":\"Story Collapsed Comments iOS\",\"variant\":\"control\"};\n    var assignments = Array.isArray(window.ldExperiments) ? window.ldExperiments : [];\n    var existingIndex = assignments.findIndex(function (item) {\n        return item.name === assignment.name;\n    });\n    var isNewAssignment = existingIndex === -1\n        || assignments[existingIndex].variant !== assignment.variant;\n\n    if (existingIndex === -1) {\n        assignments.push(assignment);\n    } else {\n        assignments[existingIndex] = assignment;\n    }\n\n    window.ldExperiments = assignments;\n    window.ldExpName = assignment.name;\n    window.ldExpVar = assignment.variant;\n\n    if (isNewAssignment) {\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\n        window.dataLayer.push({\n            event: \"experiment_assignment\",\n            experiment_name: assignment.name,\n            experiment_variant: assignment.variant\n        });\n    }\n}());","id":"collapsed-comments-ios-experiment-tracking"}])</script><script id="story-json-ld" type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"NewsArticle","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sabrina Maggiore"},"description":"It&rsquo;s more than just a bad smell that residents say is traveling from the Meadow Branch Landfill and seeping into their homes at night. Athens residents say they believe Landfill gas is making them sick. \"When it comes in the house, we get ringing in our ears, and my son and a couple of nights where it was really bad in the house, his nose actually started bleeding,\" says Spring Creek Cove resident Katie Toth. It&rsquo;s a problem residents at Spring Creek Cove have documented for quite some time. ","headline":"'His nose started bleeding:' Athens residents say landfill odor is making them sick","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"WTVC","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/assets/wtvc/images/logos/wtvc-logo.svg"}},"speakable":{"@type":"SpeakableSpecification","xpath":["//div[contains(@class, 'StoryText_storyText')]//p"]},"thumbnailUrl":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/b7afa785-95aa-4fa3-909a-136594740451-jumbo16x9_thumb_25472.png?1645746651257","wordCount":650,"image":[{"@type":"ImageObject","caption":"WTVC","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/b7afa785-95aa-4fa3-909a-136594740451-jumbo16x9_thumb_25472.png?1645746651257","width":"1280","height":"720"},{"@type":"ImageObject","caption":"WTVC","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/b7afa785-95aa-4fa3-909a-136594740451-jumbo1x1_thumb_25472.png?1645746656962","width":"720","height":"720"},{"@type":"ImageObject","caption":"WTVC","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/b7afa785-95aa-4fa3-909a-136594740451-jumbo16x9_thumb_25472.png?1645746651257","width":"1280","height":"720"},{"@type":"ImageObject","caption":"WTVC","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/b7afa785-95aa-4fa3-909a-136594740451-jumbo1x1_thumb_25472.png?1645746656962","width":"720","height":"720"},{"@type":"ImageObject","caption":"WTVC","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/71a1821b-5ee6-4d68-ba80-a5429b32cb2c-jumbo16x9_thumb_63837.png?1645746683661","width":"1280","height":"720"},{"@type":"ImageObject","caption":"WTVC","url":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/71a1821b-5ee6-4d68-ba80-a5429b32cb2c-jumbo1x1_thumb_63837.png?1645746689746","width":"720","height":"720"}],"mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://newschannel9.com/news/local/his-nose-started-bleeding-athens-residents-say-landfill-odor-is-making-them-sick","@type":"WebPage","name":"'His nose started bleeding:' Athens residents say landfill odor is making them sick"},"url":"https://newschannel9.com/news/local/his-nose-started-bleeding-athens-residents-say-landfill-odor-is-making-them-sick","articleBody":"It&rsquo;s more than just a bad smell that residents say is traveling from the Meadow Branch Landfill and seeping into their homes at night. Athens residents say they believe Landfill gas is making them sick. \"When it comes in the house, we get ringing in our ears, and my son and a couple of nights where it was really bad in the house, his nose actually started bleeding,\" says Spring Creek Cove resident Katie Toth. It&rsquo;s a problem residents at Spring Creek Cove have documented for quite some time. \"It's definitely causing issues with the residents,\" says Paul Semenoff. TDEC&rsquo;s website shows 8 new complaints for the landfill in just the last week. According to TDEC, they regularly inspect complaints and did find a violation for excessive leachate levels after a February 10th inspection. \"I get phone calls and emails constantly from from people in the area from the county,\" says McMinn County Commissioner Tad Simpson. Simpson says since we first reported on the landfill in December the complaints have continued. \"They said that they were going to work really hard to be a good neighbor to us. And I still don't find them being a good neighbor,\" saysToth. She says communication from the landfill to residents stopped some time ago. \"February 9th was the last time that we heard back from landfill management,\" said Toth. We wanted to know what steps the landfill was taking to address resident concerns and repeatedly tried to contact the landfill over the last week. After finally connecting with general manager Tim Fadul Thursday, he told us he had \"no comment at this time.\" As residents here have continued to report complaints, the county is now looking towards taking things into their own hands and possibly hiring a third party monitoring system. Mayor John Gentry told NewsChannel 9 that the county is waiting on a proposal to come in from a monitoring system known as \"Envirosuite\" According to the county mayor, they want to be able to determine if harmful gases and pollutants like methane or carbon dioxide are escaping the landfill. \"The third party monitoring is just an accountability thing. It's not the, like I said, it's not the end all there's, there's so much more,\" says Semenoff. \"It needs to be addressed. Now, Meadow Branch says that they're trying to fix it. And hopefully with this third party monitoring, if the county's able to do it, maybe it'll be another tool,\" said Simpson. For residents like Katie Toth and Paul Semenoff, it's a problem that needs to be addressed sooner rather than later. \"I just really want them to fix the problem, I would love to have fresh air back. I am tired of having to worry about my family,\" says Toth. View TDEC's recent statement on complaints from the landfill below: TDEC continues to perform complaint investigations and scheduled inspections at the landfill. A violation was assigned on Feb. 15, 2022 following an inspection on Feb. 10 that found excessive leachate levels &ndash; see attached. A contractor was onsite during the inspection to add an additional sump pump to get the issue back into compliance. Interim cover was also observed during the Feb. 10 inspection, which is in addition to the required one foot of interim cover already in place. The facility continues to use six inches of soil at the working face at the end of each day. Regarding air monitoring &ndash; the source emissions test on the leachate evaporator is scheduled to take place on March 1, 2022. TDEC has ordered analyzing equipment and it is expected to arrive by mid-March. Federal Tier II testing is required every five years. The last Tier II test was performed on July 11, 2017, therefore Tier II testing must be completed again by the end of 2022. TDEC has requested that Meadow Branch complete the testing earlier than required. - TDEC Spokesperson","articleSection":"Local","keywords":"news, waste, athens,greece, john gentry, athens, environmental soil science, local, landfill, paul semenoff, tim fadul, physical sciences, tad simpson, envirosuite, envirosuite limited, anaerobic digestion, leachate, katie toth, waste management, newsletter daily","dateModified":"2022-02-25T00:42:39.000-05:00","datePublished":"2022-02-24T18:53:17.000-05:00","video":{"@type":"VideoObject","embedUrl":"https://sinclair-vod-assets.sinclairstoryline.com/ce2a1184f08646938dcdb400a555f843/ce2a1184f08646938dcdb400a555f843.mp4","name":"'His nose started bleeding:' Athens residents say landfill odor is making them sick","duration":"PT2M34S","description":"It&rsquo;s more than just a bad smell that residents say is traveling from the Meadow Branch Landfill and seeping into their homes at night. Athens residents say they believe Landfill gas is making them sick. \"When it comes in the house, we get ringing in our ears, and my son and a couple of nights where it was really bad in the house, his nose actually started bleeding,\" says Spring Creek Cove resident Katie Toth. It&rsquo;s a problem residents at Spring Creek Cove have documented for quite some time. ","thumbnailUrl":"https://newschannel9.com/resources/media/71a1821b-5ee6-4d68-ba80-a5429b32cb2c-thumb_63837.png","uploadDate":"2022-02-24T18:53:17.000-05:00"}}</script><div id="main-content"><div><div class="InfiniteScroll_container__7G7pl"><div style="position:relative;z-index:1"><div class="StoryPage_storyPage__JhcXf" data-story-analytic-data="{&quot;article_name&quot;:&quot;&#x27;His nose started bleeding:&#x27; Athens residents say landfill odor is making them sick&quot;,&quot;article_pos&quot;:&quot;page_0&quot;,&quot;article_sections&quot;:[&quot;news&quot;,&quot;local&quot;],&quot;article_tags&quot;:[&quot;Athens&quot;,&quot;Athens,Greece&quot;,&quot;ENVIROSUITE LIMITED&quot;,&quot;envirosuite&quot;,&quot;Tad Simpson&quot;,&quot;John Gentry&quot;,&quot;Paul Semenoff&quot;,&quot;Katie Toth&quot;,&quot;Tim Fadul&quot;,&quot;Anaerobic Digestion&quot;,&quot;Environmental Soil Science&quot;,&quot;Landfill&quot;,&quot;Leachate&quot;,&quot;Physical Sciences&quot;,&quot;Waste&quot;,&quot;Waste Management&quot;],&quot;article_uuid&quot;:&quot;0a1910bb-3b6c-4619-af3f-7df9ae6d1249&quot;,&quot;author_name&quot;:&quot;Sabrina Maggiore&quot;,&quot;publish_date&quot;:&quot;2022-02-25T00:42:39.000-05:00&quot;,&quot;syndicated_paths&quot;:[],&quot;served_from&quot;:&quot;direct&quot;}" data-story-embed-count="2" data-story-embed-types="hero_video:1,video:1" data-story-focus="Athens" data-story-title="&#x27;His nose started bleeding:&#x27; Athens residents say landfill odor is making them sick" data-story-url="/news/local/his-nose-started-bleeding-athens-residents-say-landfill-odor-is-making-them-sick" data-story-uuid="0a1910bb-3b6c-4619-af3f-7df9ae6d1249"><div class="StoryPage_storyTopAdContainer__6udZ0 StoryPage_storyTopAdContainerPrimisPadding__3pdZS"><div class="Breakpoints_fallbackWrapperDefault__4Pzjc Breakpoints_display-S-only__HbxV8 Breakpoints_display-M-only__ABnKP Breakpoints_display-L-only__s1GQt Breakpoints_display-XL-only__hEcw3"><div style="height:101px"></div></div><div class="Breakpoints_fallbackWrapperDefault__4Pzjc Breakpoints_display-XS-only__cyBqQ"><div style="height:61px"></div></div></div><div class="PageColumn_pageColumn__21k88"><div class="StickyTwoColumn_twoColumns___4WPy"><div class="StickyTwoColumn_leftColumn__EmK0K StoryPage_leftColumn__GqF6y"><div class="Panel_panel__wT2cw"><div class="StoryPage_storyContainer__MLE71"><h1 class="StoryPage_headline__AP3j8">&#x27;His nose started bleeding:&#x27; Athens residents say landfill odor is making them sick</h1><hr/><div class="ByLineContainer_storyBylineContainer__0JNT7" id="js-Story-Byline-0"><div><p class="ByLine_storyByLineText__cze7l">by<!-- --> <!-- -->Sabrina Maggiore</p><time class="ByLineContainer_storyDatelineText__yS9e8" dateTime="2022-02-24 18:53">Thu, February 24, 2022 at 6:53 PM</time><div class="ByLineContainer_storyDatelineText__yS9e8"><span class="ByLineContainer_updatedText__0D6FY">Updated </span><time dateTime="2022-02-25 00:42">Fri, February 25, 2022 at 12:42 AM</time></div></div><button class="UserWayButton_userWayButton__h8S9a ByLineContainer_userWayButton___vCFL"><img alt="UserWay icon for accessibility widget" height="26" src="/resources/defaults/news_3.0/icons/accessibility/userway-transparent.svg" width="26"/></button></div><div class="StoryPage_heroContainer__6ClhH"><div><div class="StoryHero_hero__lQrxr"><span class="StoryHero_hero__lQrxr"><span class="MaxVideoPlayer_videoContainer__Pay10"><img alt="thumb_25472.png" class="MaxVideoPlayer_posterUnderlay__SDwyv" decoding="async" fetchPriority="high" loading="eager" src="/resources/media2/16x9/full/800/center/80/b7afa785-95aa-4fa3-909a-136594740451-large16x9_thumb_25472.png"/><span class="MaxVideoPlayer_videoPlayer__2SPAo hero-vod-wrapper-0a1910bb-3b6c-4619-af3f-7df9ae6d1249"><span id="player-1765"></span></span><div class="Spinner_wrapper__HoyGK Spinner_show__ZZ8CT MaxVideoPlayer_loadingSpinner__gvNZm"><div class="Spinner_spinner__EV01_"></div></div></span></span></div><div class="StoryHero_caption__eOw9W"><div>WTVC</div></div></div></div><div class="StoryPage_storyTextBlockContainer__LUkwY"><div class="StoryControls_controls__pSYQ_ StoryPage_controlsContainer__StRFl"><div class="Comment_commentWrapper__cGs3_ StoryPage_controlsContainer__StRFl"><div class="Comment_bubbleContainer__I9Tld"><button aria-label="Comment on this story" class="BaseButton_baseButton__PZJj9" type="button"><div class="BaseButton_buttonContent__3ERR7 Comment_commentGap__lJbAn"><span class="BaseButton_icon__9pZM8"><svg height="28px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 42 42" width="28px" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><title>Comment on this story</title><g fill="none" fill-rule="evenodd" id="Page-1" stroke="none" stroke-width="1"><g fill="#FFFFFF" id="L-|-Story-Detail---Commenting" stroke="#121212" transform="translate(-214.000000, -907.000000)"><g id="Group" transform="translate(215.000000, 908.000000)"><path d="M7.30803419,33.8461538 C5.25675214,33.8461538 3.52547009,33.1897436 2.11692308,31.874188 C0.705641026,30.5613675 0,28.9422222 0,27.0194872 L0,6.92239316 C0,4.99965812 0.705641026,3.36410256 2.11692308,2.01846154 C3.52547009,0.672820513 5.25675214,0 7.30803419,0 L32.6919658,0 C34.7432479,0 36.4745299,0.672820513 37.885812,2.01846154 C39.294359,3.36410256 40,4.99965812 40,6.92239316 L40,27.0194872 C40,28.9422222 39.294359,30.5613675 37.885812,31.874188 C36.4745299,33.1897436 34.7432479,33.8461538 32.6919658,33.8461538 L32.3090598,33.8461538 L32.3090598,40 C27.2437607,36.5374359 24.4868376,34.6475214 24.0382906,34.3275214 C23.5897436,34.0075214 22.9169231,33.8461538 22.0198291,33.8461538 L7.30803419,33.8461538 Z" id="sbg-comment"></path></g></g></g></svg><span class="Comment_commentCount__I6yAX">0</span></span><span class="BaseButton_label__jyklb Comment_commentLabel__cnGR6">Comment</span></div></button></div></div><button aria-label="Share story" class="BaseButton_baseButton__PZJj9 StoryPage_controlsContainer__StRFl" type="button"><div class="BaseButton_buttonContent__3ERR7"><span class="BaseButton_icon__9pZM8"><svg height="22px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 27 22" width="27px" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><title>Share story</title><g fill="none" fill-rule="evenodd" id="Design-V6" stroke="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1"><g id="UI-Elements" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1.2" transform="translate(-174, -226)"><g id="Group-7-Copy-3" transform="translate(174, 227)"><g id="Share" transform="translate(1.5, 0)"><path d="M24.000048,7.19038119 L13.9941255,0 L13.9941255,3.62430582 C-0.889019116,3.62430582 0.0104599993,20 0.0104599993,20 C0.0104599993,20 2.19550555,10.7564566 13.9941255,10.7564566 L13.9941255,14.3807624 L24.000048,7.19038119 Z" id="Stroke-1"></path></g></g></g></g></svg></span><span class="BaseButton_label__jyklb">Share</span></div></button></div><div class="StoryPage_contentColumnContainer__fMqAt"><div class="StoryPage_taboolaDeeperDive__WKVX7" data-url="https://newschannel9.com/news/local/his-nose-started-bleeding-athens-residents-say-landfill-odor-is-making-them-sick" id="deeper-dive-container-0"></div><div class="TopicsBar_topicsBar__eU8Uv StoryPage_topicsContainer__YIZ_i"><ul class="TopicsBar_topicsContainer__GzlWc"><h4 class="TopicsBar_title__YlW20">topics: </h4><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/Athens">Athens</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/Athens%2CGreece">Athens,Greece</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/ENVIROSUITE%20LIMITED">ENVIROSUITE LIMITED</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/envirosuite">envirosuite</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/Tad%20Simpson">Tad Simpson</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/John%20Gentry">John Gentry</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/Paul%20Semenoff">Paul Semenoff</a></li><li class="TopicsBar_topic__8UfR4"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TopicsBar_aTag__uumvE" href="/topic/Katie%20Toth">Katie Toth</a></li></ul></div><div class="StoryPage_divider__ZF7oD"></div><div class="StoryText_storyText__C3hWI StoryText_storyText__C3hWI"><div><p><span class="dateline">ATHENS, Tenn. — </span>It’s more than just a bad smell that residents say is traveling from the Meadow Branch Landfill and seeping into their homes at night. Athens residents say they believe  Landfill gas is making them sick.</p><blockquote>&quot;When it comes in the house, we get ringing in our ears, and my son and a couple of nights where it was really bad in the house, his nose actually started bleeding,&quot; says Spring Creek Cove resident Katie Toth.</blockquote><p>It’s a problem residents at Spring Creek Cove have documented for quite some time.<span class="extraSpace"></span></p><div class="PrimisMidArticleAdUnit_mobile__XQxD4 PrimisMidArticleAdUnit_primisWrapper__G3UAH"><div class="PrimisMidArticleAdUnit_advertisementTag__2bPJb"></div><div id="primis-mid-story-ad-0-anchor-mobile"></div></div><blockquote>&quot;It&#x27;s definitely causing issues with the residents,&quot; says Paul Semenoff.</blockquote><p>TDEC’s website shows 8 new complaints for the landfill in just the last week.</p><div class="PrimisMidArticleAdUnit_desktop__dq_iB PrimisMidArticleAdUnit_primisWrapper__G3UAH"><div class="PrimisMidArticleAdUnit_advertisementTag__2bPJb"></div><div id="primis-mid-story-ad-0-anchor-desktop"></div></div><p>According to TDEC, they regularly inspect complaints and did find a violation for excessive leachate levels after a February 10th inspection.</p><blockquote>&quot;I get phone calls and emails constantly from from people in the area from the county,&quot; says McMinn County Commissioner Tad Simpson.</blockquote><p>Simpson says since we first reported on the landfill in December the complaints have continued.</p><blockquote>&quot;They said that they were going to work really hard to be a good neighbor to us. And I still don&#x27;t find them being a good neighbor,&quot; saysToth.</blockquote><p>She says communication from the landfill to residents stopped some time ago.</p><p>&quot;February 9th was the last time that we heard back from landfill management,&quot; said Toth.</p><p>We wanted to know what steps the landfill was taking to address resident concerns and repeatedly tried to contact the landfill over the last week. After finally connecting with general manager Tim Fadul Thursday, he told us he had &quot;no comment at this time.&quot;<span class="extraSpace"></span></p><p>As residents here have continued to report complaints, the county is now looking towards taking things into their own hands and possibly hiring a third party monitoring system.</p><p>Mayor John Gentry told NewsChannel 9 that the county is waiting on a proposal to come in from a monitoring system known as &quot;Envirosuite&quot;<span class="extraSpace"></span></p><p>According to the county mayor, they want to be able to determine if harmful gases and pollutants like methane or carbon dioxide are escaping the landfill.</p><blockquote>&quot;The third party monitoring is just an accountability thing. It&#x27;s not the, like I said, it&#x27;s not the end all there&#x27;s, there&#x27;s so much more,&quot; says Semenoff.</blockquote><p>&quot;It needs to be addressed. Now, Meadow Branch says that they&#x27;re trying to fix it. And hopefully with this third party monitoring, if the county&#x27;s able to do it, maybe it&#x27;ll be another tool,&quot; said Simpson.</p><p><span class="VideoEmbed_videoEmbed__Qn_0f"><span class="VideoEmbed_videoContainer__Pe1Y5"><span class="VideoEmbed_placeholder__5VC9v"><span class="VideoEmbed_spinner__oFTUn"></span></span></span><span class="VideoEmbed_caption__o_5xL"><div>WTVC</div></span></span></p><p>For residents like Katie Toth and Paul Semenoff, it&#x27;s a problem that needs to be addressed sooner rather than later.</p><p>&quot;I just really want them to fix the problem, I would love to have fresh air back. I am tired of having to worry about my family,&quot; says Toth.<br/></p><p>View TDEC&#x27;s recent statement on complaints from the landfill below:<span class="extraSpace"></span></p><p><em>TDEC continues to perform complaint investigations and scheduled inspections at the landfill. A violation was assigned on Feb. 15, 2022 following an inspection on Feb. 10 that found excessive leachate levels – see attached. A contractor was onsite during the inspection to add an additional sump pump to get the issue back into compliance. Interim cover was also observed during the Feb. 10 inspection, which is in addition to the required one foot of interim cover already in place. The facility continues to use six inches of soil at the working face at the end of each day.</em></p><p><em>Regarding air monitoring – the source emissions test on the leachate evaporator is scheduled to take place on March 1, 2022. TDEC has ordered analyzing equipment and it is expected to arrive by mid-March. Federal Tier II testing is required every five years. The last Tier II test was performed on July 11, 2017, therefore Tier II testing must be completed again by the end of 2022. TDEC has requested that Meadow Branch complete the testing earlier than required. - TDEC Spokesperson</em></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="TaboolaMoreToExplore_taboolaContainerWrapper__Ccf_j"><div id="taboola-0a1910bb-3b6c-4619-af3f-7df9ae6d1249"></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="StoryCommentingSection_lazyLoadSentinel__POpRG" data-testid="openweb-lazy-load-sentinel" id="js-openWebConversation-Container_0" style="height:1px;width:100%"></div></div></div><div class="StickyTwoColumn_rightColumn__vCmRf"><div class="StoryPage_rightColumn__t9tAM"><div class="Panel_panel__wT2cw"><div class="Breakpoints_fallbackWrapperDefault__4Pzjc Breakpoints_display-XS-only__cyBqQ Breakpoints_display-S-only__HbxV8 Breakpoints_display-M-only__ABnKP Breakpoints_display-L-only__s1GQt Breakpoints_display-XL-only__hEcw3"><div style="height:681px"></div></div></div><div class="TeasersBlockSidebar_teaserBlock__wUrKC Panel_panel__wT2cw"><h2 class="TeasersBlockSidebar_teasersTitle__hJZ_x">Trending</h2><div class="TeasersBlockSidebar_teasers__swsOT"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TeaserLink_teaserLink__p1kuV TeaserLink_sidebarPrimary__CoLUx" href="/news/local/tennessee-governor-halts-executions-after-christa-gail-pike-survives-lethal-injection?teaserSource=trending"><picture class="TeaserLink_teaserPicture__kW5wk"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchPriority="auto" height="197" loading="lazy" src="/resources/media2/16x9/691/648/1x0/90/4a3d5391-a1ba-4c00-9a13-34cc46156545-BillLeeChristaPike.png" width="351"/></picture><div class="TeaserLink_teaserText__g1DQc"><div>Tennessee governor halts executions after Christa Gail Pike survives lethal injection</div><span class="TeaserLink_galleryIcon__W3OjR"></span></div><div class="TeaserLink_teaserSummary__nulFo">NASHVILLE, Tenn. (AP) &amp;mdash; Tennessee officials were unable to put Christa Gail Pike to death Wednesday for a 1995 murder after administering two doses of a lethal</div></a><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TeaserLink_teaserLink__p1kuV TeaserLink_sidebarSecondary__CkQRW" href="/news/local/failed-tennessee-execution-renews-the-debate-over-death-penalty-methods?teaserSource=trending"><picture class="TeaserLink_teaserPicture__kW5wk"><source height="56" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/5103/648/0x266/90/fb020ef1-8c51-4187-b1aa-2bcf5ebe1bd1-AP26274087311818.jpg" width="100"/><source height="56" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/5103/648/0x266/90/fb020ef1-8c51-4187-b1aa-2bcf5ebe1bd1-AP26274087311818.jpg" width="100"/><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchPriority="auto" height="100" loading="lazy" src="/resources/media2/1x1/3402/200/851x0/90/fb020ef1-8c51-4187-b1aa-2bcf5ebe1bd1-AP26274087311818.jpg" width="100"/></picture><div class="TeaserLink_teaserText__g1DQc"><div>Failed Tennessee execution renews the debate over death penalty methods</div><span class="TeaserLink_galleryIcon__W3OjR"></span></div><div class="TeaserLink_teaserSummary__nulFo">Tennessee officials have yet to explain what went wrong during the failed execution of Christa Pike, which was called off after she was given two doses of the d</div></a><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TeaserLink_teaserLink__p1kuV TeaserLink_sidebarSecondary__CkQRW" href="/news/local/tennessee-unable-to-carry-out-execution-of-christa-pike-witnesses-say?teaserSource=trending"><picture class="TeaserLink_teaserPicture__kW5wk"><source height="56" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/808/648/25x0/90/d9559cf2-10c6-4e7f-852e-629310fbaacc-CHRISTAPIKE.png" width="100"/><source height="56" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/808/648/25x0/90/d9559cf2-10c6-4e7f-852e-629310fbaacc-CHRISTAPIKE.png" width="100"/><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchPriority="auto" height="100" loading="lazy" src="/resources/media2/1x1/455/200/201x0/90/d9559cf2-10c6-4e7f-852e-629310fbaacc-CHRISTAPIKE.png" width="100"/></picture><div class="TeaserLink_teaserText__g1DQc"><div>Tennessee unable to carry out execution by lethal injection, Christa Pike hospitalized</div><span class="TeaserLink_galleryIcon__W3OjR"></span></div><div class="TeaserLink_teaserSummary__nulFo">Tennessee officials were unable to carry out the execution of Christa Gail Pike for a 1995 murder on Wednesday, media witnesses said.</div></a><div class="ViewportBufferedSlot_shell__7Nkhq" data-slot-label="DisplayAd adName=ddb_fluid_native adIndex=0 pageType=story placement=Native trendingSidebar" data-testid="viewport-buffered-slot" data-viewport-buffered="false" data-viewport-in-buffer="false" style="min-height:250px"><div class="RightRailTrendingAd_nativeAdWrapper__dxc78"><div class="DisplayAd_Native__XCll3 native"><div><div id="ddb_fluid_native_ddb_0"></div></div></div></div></div><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TeaserLink_teaserLink__p1kuV TeaserLink_sidebarSecondary__CkQRW" href="/news/local/colbin-davis-to-face-murder-charge-in-michaels-road-shooting-case-sheriffs-office-says?teaserSource=trending"><picture class="TeaserLink_teaserPicture__kW5wk"><source height="56" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/1920/648/center/90/b508af5a-3626-4bc1-82fc-d7c37a4c1ea4-Colbindaviswebphoto.jpg" width="100"/><source height="56" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/1920/648/center/90/b508af5a-3626-4bc1-82fc-d7c37a4c1ea4-Colbindaviswebphoto.jpg" width="100"/><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchPriority="auto" height="100" loading="lazy" src="/resources/media2/1x1/1080/200/420x0/90/b508af5a-3626-4bc1-82fc-d7c37a4c1ea4-Colbindaviswebphoto.jpg" width="100"/></picture><div class="TeaserLink_teaserText__g1DQc"><div>Sheriff: Dade County man to face murder charge in Michael&#x27;s Road shooting case</div><span class="TeaserLink_galleryIcon__W3OjR"></span><span class="TeaserLink_videoIcon__vD91T"></span></div><div class="TeaserLink_teaserSummary__nulFo">The suspect in the Michael&#x27;s Road shooting on Tuesday will now face a murder charge, according to the Dade County Sheriff&#x27;s Office.</div></a><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr TeaserLink_teaserLink__p1kuV TeaserLink_sidebarSecondary__CkQRW" href="/news/local/driver-found-dead-in-submerged-truck-after-crash-on-birchwood-pike-saturday-identified?teaserSource=trending"><picture class="TeaserLink_teaserPicture__kW5wk"><source height="56" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/1920/648/0x100/90/688f7ff0-bcec-4c5c-a993-fd27a15f042a-HCSOCARGENERIC.png" width="100"/><source height="56" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="/resources/media2/16x9/1920/648/0x100/90/688f7ff0-bcec-4c5c-a993-fd27a15f042a-HCSOCARGENERIC.png" width="100"/><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchPriority="auto" height="100" loading="lazy" src="/resources/media2/1x1/1279/200/321x0/90/688f7ff0-bcec-4c5c-a993-fd27a15f042a-HCSOCARGENERIC.png" width="100"/></picture><div class="TeaserLink_teaserText__g1DQc"><div>Driver found dead in submerged truck after crash on Birchwood Pike Saturday identified</div></div><div class="TeaserLink_teaserSummary__nulFo">The Hamilton County Sheriff&#x27;s Office says they have identified a person who was pronounced dead after deputies found them in a submerged truck on Saturday. </div></a></div></div><div class="StoryPage_bottomMobileAd__vek9s Panel_panel__wT2cw"><div class="Breakpoints_fallbackWrapperDefault__4Pzjc Breakpoints_display-XS-only__cyBqQ Breakpoints_display-S-only__HbxV8 Breakpoints_display-M-only__ABnKP Breakpoints_display-L-only__s1GQt Breakpoints_display-XL-only__hEcw3"><div style="height:281px"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="StoryPage_photoGalleryBarContainer__36YKT"><div class="PhotoGalleryBar_container__NbpZN"><div class="PhotoGalleryBar_pageWidth__sCIsw"><div class="PhotoGalleryBar_header__gLsiK"><h2 class="PhotoGalleryBar_title___ZjLx">NEWS IN PHOTOS:</h2><span class="PhotoGalleryBar_subtitle__s9wtM">&quot;<!-- -->Local<!-- -->&quot;</span></div><div class="PhotoGalleryBar_galleryGrid__8tciB"><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr PhotoGalleryBarLink_galleryLink__NpV9Q PhotoGalleryBar_galleryItem__G_Jvh" href="/news/local/gallery/new-denso-solar-field-offsets-nearly-14-of-athens-plant-power-use" data-title-position="below"><div class="PhotoGalleryBarLink_imageContainer__b90JO"><img alt="Image for gallery: New DENSO solar field offsets nearly 14% of Athens plant power use" aria-hidden="true" class="PhotoGalleryBarLink_image___vKEb" height="203" src="/resources/media2/16x9/2667/648/0x250/90/f98a36ec-afde-4c93-adee-7faeb41c9051-4305126DensoDMATDMTN75.jpg" width="360"/><div class="PhotoGalleryBarLink_imageMask__DTkJV"></div><span class="PhotoGalleryBarLink_imageCount__ObzT0">3</span></div><div class="PhotoGalleryBarLink_belowTitleContainer__EaAVz"><span class="PhotoGalleryBarLink_belowTitleText__03CN2">New DENSO solar field offsets nearly 14% of Athens plant power use</span></div></a><a class="Link_link__1Aqdr PhotoGalleryBarLink_galleryLink__NpV9Q PhotoGalleryBar_galleryItem__G_Jvh" href="/news/local/gallery/christa-pike-says-she-feels-a-kinship-with-lindsay-clancy-before-failed-execution-tennessee-death-row-inmate-murder-conv